lessons (chained-transfers): 10 live; adopted first. Status is derived from tests.
- [adopted +59/-0] L-77b44d3fe205 (*): when writing or editing a PR body -> run python3 tools/pcc/pcc.py lint-prose --stdin on it before submitting; reword claim words for proposals or cite [pcc:ID]
- [adopted +29/-0] L-1e09e78e395f (*): when writing today's session log -> fetch origin/main first and append to the existing same-day file; other sessions write the same file and an add/add conflict blocks merge
- [adopted +9/-0] L-5b0291c61e8e (*): when Merging an append-only shared journal with repeated section headings -> Compare and preserve full normalized blocks as a multiset, retaining their multiplicities; headings are not unique keys. Preserve existing chronology and review source pins before applying a prepared merge.
- [adopted +2/-0] L-8d86e8fc352c (*): when correcting a results file whose hash a VALIDATION.json or validator report pins -> leave the pinned file byte-equal and put the corrections in a sibling ERRATA.md that the PROOF/problem notes cite; editing it in place makes the gate report a sha256 mismatch
- [candidate +1/-0] L-969990a5f5ba (*): when A tool orchestration validates text before a dependent publication or mutation -> Check the validation exit status and end the script on nonzero before invoking the mutation; use explicit early exit or a guarded shell && chain. Keep independent read batching separate.
- [candidate +0/-0] L-dbdd5a9d8530 (*): when restarting a work branch whose PR merged with a merge commit -> git checkout -B <branch> origin/main (carry uncommitted work with git stash) and push normally: the old remote head is an ancestor of main, so the push fast-forwards; no force push is needed
- [candidate +0/-0] L-306254ce1b4a (*): when a generator scans a file that also contains its own generated output (e.g. tools/artifacts/wire_workflows.py and the pull step it writes into workflows) -> strip the generated block before discovery and declare indirect inputs explicitly; otherwise an entry the tool once wrote counts as a reference to itself and never drops out
- [candidate +0/-0] L-85f1696fa884 (*): when editing or writing tests in a Rust source file that another crate includes with #[path] (e.g. src/binary_ecc/f2m.rs in research/quadratic_twist_evidence_20261021/native/metadata) -> use relative super:: paths, never crate::<module>:: paths, and build the including crate too
- [candidate +0/-0] L-97bc69de5096 (*): when fixing the first failing step of a CI job that has been red for a while -> expect later steps to have been masked: after the fix lands, read the next run's log to the end before calling the job fixed
- [candidate +0/-0] L-03e1d0d51c4d (*): when Creating a PCC claim in a fresh sparse checkout -> Materialize the tracked pcc ledger and keyring from the pinned base before invoking claim new; verify the base prefix before publication.
  outcomes chained-transfers: 0/1 success (95% CI 0.00-0.79)
